{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"unmedical-stational-chrysalis","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\nOn 2026-10-28 the on-box MCP container (`rebar-mcp-e2ed08b343a2-8092`, limit 3,892,314,112 bytes) went from 0.93 GB resident (`rebar-health` sample 15:29:23 PDT) to 3.28 GB (15:34:23 PDT) and stayed between 3.16 and 3.41 GB for 2 hours 12 minutes, until the kernel OOM-killed it at 17:47:26 PDT when a batch of concurrent reads arrived (bug teenage-unquieted-ringworm).\n\nThe container log with timestamps (`docker logs -t`) shows tool calls (`CallToolRequest`) between 15:22 and 15:29:40 PDT, including plan-review gate activity (an admission warning for pyrite-cockeyed-gannet at 15:26:52). From 15:29:40 to 15:38 it shows only `PingRequest`. So the 2.3 GB rise happened with no request in flight.\n\nFor comparison, measured in the MCP image on Linux: 9 concurrent `next_batch` calls return their memory afterwards (peak 4,966 MB, 201 MB after), and a second burst peaks no higher than the first. Store-wide reads do not explain a plateau that lasts hours.\n\n## Not established\n\nWhat held the memory. Candidates to test: a background gate job (`review_plan_start` / `verify_completion_start` run on a daemon thread and outlive the request), a detached post-close compaction worker, or another child process inside the container. `rebar-health` samples container-wide RSS, so a child process counts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The process or thread holding the memory during a plateau is identified with evidence (for example `docker top` plus per-process RSS, or a per-job memory log) and recorded here.\n- [ ] Either the holder releases its memory when its work ends, or its memory is bounded and documented against the container limit.\n- [ ] A test or probe that would fail if a finished background job keeps its memory.","id":"e152-4009-4180-4fd8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP container holds about 2.3 GB for hours after background work with no request in flight"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793238033093453001,"uuid":"cebc08fd-206d-46d7-ac91-fc48dc1c917e"}